// Creatures. Models are boxes in creature space: metres, y up, -z is the way it faces.
//   temper:  Skittish (runs from you), Neutral (fights back when hit), Hostile (hunts you),
//            Spirit (drifts through walls at night, kept back by torchlight), Villager
//   health, speed (walking, blocks/s), run (fleeing or chasing)
//   size:    (width, height) of its body, for hits and collisions
//   attack:  damage, cause (Blunt, Piercing or Chill: which health bar it starts on),
//            reach (blocks) and every (seconds between blows)
//   spawn:   where and when it appears: biomes (names from biomes.ron; empty = any land),
//            when: Day, Night or Any; at: Surface or Barrow; group: (min, max); weight
//   drops:   [(item, count, chance)]
//   glow:    a ghostly light colour (sRGB), drawn see-through
//   skin:    a PNG in assets/textures/creatures/ painted onto the model (skins: [...] picks one
//            at random per creature). `cargo run --bin creature_skins` writes a starter PNG and a
//            guide for any listed skin that doesn't exist yet. Without a skin the boxes use `color`.
//   model:   boxes: name (for animation later), size, offset, color (flat colour / starter fill),
//            uv: (x, y) to pin the box's patch in the skin (otherwise packed in list order:
//            add new boxes at the end so painted ones don't move)
[
    (
        name: "marsh_boar", title: "Marsh Boar", temper: Neutral, health: 24.0, speed: 1.8, run: 4.6,
        size: (0.9, 0.9),
        skin: "marsh_boar",
        model: [
            (name: "body",            size: (0.8, 0.6, 1.2), offset: (0.0, 0.55, 0.0), color: (0.36, 0.27, 0.2)),
